@kstellana explains the problem to @HenriArslanian in this clip.

Two agents can automate a whole deal. But when one says the work was bad, the contract cannot go and check. The first disagreement freezes everything, and no court exists for that moment.

@GenLayer is built for that gap. Validators running different AI models reach consensus on questions that need judgment, so a contract can settle a subjective call instead of stalling.

My take: we put huge effort into letting agents pay each other and almost none into what happens when they disagree.

